# Byte-exact text artifacts: the ledger staleness check and fixgen byte-identity
# check regenerate these and diff against the working tree, so checkouts must
# never translate line endings on them.
#
# ENFORCED-BY: this file. The rules below are the enforcement; they hold for any
# value of core.autocrlf, which is why they are stated per-path rather than
# relying on a git config.
#
# History of this comment, kept because it has been wrong twice:
#   - It once asserted "repo has core.autocrlf=true locally". Nothing enforced
#     that, and it was not true.
#   - The replacement (2026-08-16) asserted autocrlf was "unset locally and
#     globally, so no translation at all". Also wrong: only `--local` and
#     `--global` had been checked. `git config --system core.autocrlf` is
#     `true` (the Git for Windows install default), so translation IS active
#     and always has been.
# What is actually true: core.autocrlf is true via the system config, and the
# per-path rules below are the only reason the byte-exact artifacts survive it.
# Verified green under that configuration: `ledger:check`, `abi:check`,
# `tables:check`.
#
# Do not restate a developer's git config here. If a path must not be
# translated, list it below.

# W2: ledger artifacts (regenerated with LF, byte-diffed by ledger:check)
design/blocks.yml text eol=lf
design/ops.yml text eol=lf
design/diagrams/*.mmd text eol=lf
design/diagrams/*.md text eol=lf
design/contracts/*.md text eol=lf

# W3: fixgen artifacts (spec/qformats.md §11): never eol-convert.
fpga/rtl/generated/tables/*.mem -text
reference/include/zref/generated/*.hpp -text
compiler/src/generated/tables.ts -text
tests/golden/fixp/* -text
*.bin binary
# Byte-identity discipline (W4, spec/capture_format.md 6): generated outputs
# must byte-compare identically on every clone. core.autocrlf=true on Windows
# would round-trip them to CRLF and break `npm run abi:check`; pin them to LF.
spec/commands.zidl text eol=lf
tools/abi-gen/templates/** text eol=lf
compiler/src/generated/** text eol=lf
runtime/include/zhao_abi.h text eol=lf
fpga/rtl/generated/** text eol=lf
spec/generated/** text eol=lf
tests/fuzz/*.ts text eol=lf

# SHELL SCRIPTS MUST CHECK OUT WITH LF, AND THIS IS NOT A STYLE PREFERENCE.
#
# Found 2026-08-23 the first time a mutation sweep was run in a git worktree, as
# docs/OWNER_DOCKET.md requires them to be. A fresh checkout gave
# tools/sweep_*.sh CRLF endings, and the effect was SILENT rather than loud:
#
#   * the preflight parses the mutant table with `^"(.*?)"$` in MULTILINE mode,
#     and with CRLF the character before each newline is , not the closing
#     quote. It matched nothing and reported "linted 0 mutants, 0 do not build"
#     -- a clean pass over an empty set;
#   * bash reading `#!/usr/bin/env bash` and CRLF-terminated array entries
#     carries the  into every anchor, so no anchor can ever match its file.
#
# EVERY sweep in tools/ was affected, not just the new one. They had only ever
# been run in the tree they were authored in, where the working copy was already
# LF, so nothing had exercised a checkout of them.
#
# ENFORCED-BY: this rule, plus the preflight's own refusal to run on an empty
# mutant table -- a guard that lints nothing must fail, not pass.
*.sh text eol=lf
tools/*.py text eol=lf

# Committed binary evidence: never touch.
*.bin -text
*.zcap -text
*.zcorpus -text
tests/abi/golden/** -text
captures/** -text

# W6 CI fix (2026-08-15): the W5-emitted wrapper crater_ring.hpp is
# byte-compared by compiler/tests/crater_ring.test.ts on every run; a fresh
# autocrlf=true checkout translated it to CRLF and failed the gate on the
# first GitHub Actions run (run 31839033681). Same byte-identity rule as
# the W4 block above.
compiler/tests/generated/** text eol=lf

# W3.2: form frontend corpus + AST goldens (regenerated with LF, byte-diffed
# by the corpus test; CRLF checkout would shift byte-offset spans)
compiler/tests/frontend/corpus/positive/*.form text eol=lf
compiler/tests/frontend/corpus/golden/*.json text eol=lf
